post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
Browse runs in two halves: this CLI and a Chromium extension.

  1. Install the extension, which walks through the rest of the setup:
     https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/mfnicocicmmlkpjnaffgihfjhdgjkdjg
  2. Run `browse install` to add the MCP server to the agents found on this computer and pair
     the extension.

`browse install` copies this binary to ~/.local/bin/browse and writes that path into the agent
configurations, because that is the one location upstream keeps updated by downloading newer
releases itself. To let pacman own the updates instead, delete ~/.local/bin/browse after step 2
and point the `browse` command in each agent's MCP configuration at /usr/bin/browse.
EOF
}
